# File: plugin contract and lifecycle exercise suites
#
# Generated from: specs/bug-require-deliverable-dependencies-in-multi-pr-child-plans/requirements.md
# Issue: #163
# Type: Defect regression

@regression
Feature: Require deliverable dependencies in multi-PR child plans
  Multi-PR planning previously allowed prose-only task checkpoints that no independent
  child branch could consume. The fix requires every cross-child prerequisite to map
  to a whole issue whose deliverable is merged into the repository default branch.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Cross-child task and artifact prerequisites are detected
    Given a child plan references a task or artifact owned by another child
    When the multi-PR plan is validated
    Then the reference is identified as a cross-child delivery prerequisite

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Every prerequisite has a deliverable boundary
    Given a downstream child needs a prerequisite before its sibling is complete
    When the plan is finalized
    Then it requires a separate baseline issue and pull request or a whole-issue dependency

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Spec and GitHub graphs describe the same ordering
    Given a valid multi-PR child plan
    When task ownership, deliverable records, issue bodies, and dependency edges are compared
    Then they describe the same executable ordering without a prose-only midpoint dependency

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Readiness waits for a merged default-branch deliverable
    Given a required baseline has not been merged into the default branch available to a child
    When start-issue or status evaluates that child
    Then the child is not reported ready

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Existing plans expose unrepresentable checkpoints
    Given an existing umbrella contains cross-child task or artifact references
    When the supported initialized-project audit runs
    Then it reports each unrepresentable checkpoint and both supported repair shapes
    And legacy prose alone does not gate start-issue or status before an approved structured repair

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Approved manual repairs are exact and idempotent
    Given an operator approves one exact manual whole-issue dependency repair handoff
    When the operator applies the line-level repair and the audit runs again
    Then the issue and spec relationships change once and the second audit proposes no edit

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Every ready independent branch can consume its prerequisites
    Given multiple children use independent branches from the repository default branch
    When the lifecycle exercise advances them according to the generated graph
    Then every reported-ready child obtains all prerequisites from merged deliverables
